{
  "case_id": "2010-09-530",
  "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (General Neal K. Katyal)",
      "case_id": "2010-09-530",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
      "evidence_id": "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Background checks are a standard way of doing business. The Government has required them for all civil service employees since 1953 and for contractors since 2005. If the Ninth Circuit in this case held that a constitutional right to informational privacy precluded asking the questions it asked, that was wrong for two basic reasons."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-09-530",
      "confidence": 0.98,
      "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
      "evidence_id": "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0000-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We'll hear argument first this morning in Case 09-530, National Aeronautics and Space Administration v. Nelson."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (General Neal K. Katyal)",
      "case_id": "2010-09-530",
      "confidence": 0.91,
      "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
      "evidence_id": "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think that this Court in Whalen -- and there is no decision thus far that has recognized any constitutional limit on the Government's collection of information, so long as there are accompanying safeguards on the disseminations and --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (General Neal K. Katyal)",
      "case_id": "2010-09-530",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
      "evidence_id": "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our position here is that the Government can collect information so long as it is not disseminated in the employment context."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-530",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
      "evidence_id": "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What is the test -- what is the test for determining what sort of questions can be asked in the employment context? Is there any limit? Suppose the -- suppose the Government says, well, we want to know all about your diet; we want to know whether you smoke cigarettes; we want to know everything you read; we want to know what your hobbies are, what forms of entertainment you enjoy, sexual practices, every aspect of your private life, just because that gives us a better picture of who you are as an employee. Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-09-530",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
      "evidence_id": "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Are you representing to us that every employee who is rejected will know the reason?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2010-09-530",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
      "evidence_id": "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm representing that NASA has -- NASA will not and does not use this employee suitability chart to make contractor credentialing decisions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-530",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
      "evidence_id": "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Where did it come from?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2010-09-530",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
      "evidence_id": "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think as Judge Kleinfeld said, that's how law clerks are hired, and that's how baristas at Starbucks are hired. You have to ask these open-ended questions because as an employer, you don't really know what -- where the pressure points or danger spots in an individual application are."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2010-09-530",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
      "evidence_id": "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the narrow rule is what we said in our petition and what we said on the very last page of our reply brief and all throughout, which is, this Court should simply say what it said in Whalen, which is assuming that there is some sort of right to informational privacy, the -- the use of a background check with accompanying safeguards to collect information doesn't violate any constitutional right to privacy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-530",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
      "evidence_id": "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't see what the alternative, as a practical matter, is to asking this sort of open-ended question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-530",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
      "evidence_id": "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Do you see what I am getting at? I don't see how you are going to do this, other than by asking an open-ended question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-530",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
      "evidence_id": "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Are you suggesting that this is no good for Government employment? You were dealing with a contractor here, but this form, as I understand it, has been used for -- for many years for standard Government employment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stormer",
      "case_id": "2010-09-530",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
      "evidence_id": "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0002-0011",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The questions that are being asked here would not be allowed for a private employer --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-09-530",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
      "evidence_id": "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Question 42, do you have -- pardon me. Question 7 on Form 42, the -- the standard one -- do you have any adverse information about this person's employment, residence, or activities concerning, and so forth -- a violation of the law? Are you saying that private employers cannot ask that question?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-09-530",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
      "evidence_id": "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: But that was enjoined by the court below; was it not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-530",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
      "evidence_id": "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: May I ask you this question about the question on drug treatment? Would it be unconstitutional for the Government to take the position that to require an employee or applicant for employment to disclose whether this individual had violated Federal or State drug laws and take the position that if the person gave an affirmative answer that was disqualifying, would that be unconstitutional?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-530",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
      "evidence_id": "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What's really the difference between that regime and this -- and what you have here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Katyal",
      "case_id": "2010-09-530",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
      "evidence_id": "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0002-0014",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL KATYAL: And the judgment is based on the following rationale -- this is from the Petition Appendix at page 18a from the Ninth Circuit. \"If the Government's actions compel disclosure of private information, it has the burden of showing that its use of the information would advance a legitimate state interest and that its actions are narrowly tailored to meet the legitimate interest.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-09-530",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
      "evidence_id": "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0002-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Do you think there's something wrong with the Government having to explain why it seeks information? I mean, I would think that would be fairly simple in virtually every situation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-530",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
      "evidence_id": "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0002-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: How much of the information that's at issue here can be released and to whom?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-530",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
      "evidence_id": "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Is that also within the Government itself? I know the Privacy Act says the Government can't disclose, but how about checks -- I mean, we have a vast government -- checks about circulating the information within the Government?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Katyal",
      "case_id": "2010-09-530",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
      "evidence_id": "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL KATYAL: If it is for a -- if it is to further the Government purpose for which the information is collected, it can be distributed to other folks in the Government. There are restrictions on that, so -- and they're specified in the Privacy Act, and they're quite extensive. And to the extent the Court is concerned that there is something that isn't robust enough in the Privacy Act, we suggest that would -- that could wait for an as-applied challenge down the road when information is disclosed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-09-530",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
      "evidence_id": "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, General. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
